  "title": "while and break",
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "explain",
      "md": "## Stop when the counter says so\n\n`while` keeps going while a condition is true. `break` leaves early when you have a *reason* — here, when you have taken 2 south steps toward the beacon.\n\nA `while (true)` without `break` is a runaway. The runner will time out."
    },
    {
      "type": "predict",
      "id": "break-why",
      "promptMd": "Why does `break` exist in a `while (true)`?",
      "kind": "mcq",
      "choices": [
        {
          "id": "style",
          "md": "Only to look fancy"
        },
        {
          "id": "reason",
          "md": "To leave when a real condition happens inside the body"
        }
      ],
      "answer": "reason"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "id": "while-south",
      "engine": "javascript",
      "entry": "main.js",
      "promptMd": "> Walk south with `while` until you have moved twice. Use `break` or a counter.",
